{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8nu09u","slideIndex":1,"text":"My experience spans both application development and cloud delivery. On the application side, I’ve worked with Laravel, PHP, Filament and MySQL. For deployment, I’ve used Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, Docker, GitHub Actions and Linux. I’m also building my cloud-native skills through a lab using Kubernetes, Terraform and Ansible.\n\nA project that brings these areas together is a cloud-based court case management system. It is a production web application designed to organize debt-recovery case records. The application and database run on separate cloud virtual machines connected through a private network. The system also produces Sinhala-language PDF reports, and Docker with GitHub Actions supports deployment.\n\nThe project helped me see that good software depends on more than the application itself. Deployment, access, infrastructure and the needs of users all matter. It is the combination of these areas that I want to keep strengthening.\n\nSource: https://lk.linkedin.com/in/charithkalhara"}
