{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qpcbat0b","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":1130,"top":672,"width":86,"height":18},"text":"3 / 3","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":12,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#566577","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/drn5wn","slideIndex":2,"text":"Looking ahead, I want to grow toward cloud and DevOps engineering. My next steps are to deepen my understanding of cloud infrastructure, deployment automation and service reliability through hands-on projects. The cloud-native lab is one way I’m developing those skills.\n\nSecurity and responsibility are important to the kind of engineer I want to become. In my case management project, that means thinking about secure access and keeping the database on a private network. I’ve also contributed to writing about responsible use of predictive AI in healthcare, which reinforced that technology should be developed with care for the people it affects.\n\nMy direction is to build cloud systems that are useful, secure and reliable. Thank you.\n\nSource: https://lk.linkedin.com/in/charithkalhara"}